-- PAC-134 (spec docs/specs/PAC-134.md; contract contracts/features/PAC-134.md
-- section 4): the operator's address erasure (paceday-operator erase-address).
--
-- 1. paceday_go_lower(text): the database twin of Go's strings.ToLower, which
--    the one address normaliser uses (api/handlers_manager.go
--    normalizeManagerEmail; storage.NormaliseStoredAddress). The erasure
--    matches a stored value when its Go lowercasing OR its database lower()
--    equals the input's (spec section 3.3), and decides it in the database,
--    so the Go half needs a database function. Go's strings.ToLower maps every
--    code point to exactly one code point (simple case mapping; unicode
--    tables 15.0.0 in go1.26.0; 1433 code points change), so the function is:
--      - pure-ASCII text (octet_length = char_length in UTF8): lower() under
--        the "C" collation, which PostgreSQL defines as A-Z to a-z and
--        nothing else, whatever the database locale (Go does the same on
--        ASCII);
--      - any other text: one translate() over 1798 code points: every code
--        point U+0001..U+024F with its Go lowercase (identity entries
--        included, so a character of a common address is found near the
--        start of the list), then every higher code point Go changes.
--    Built from chr() of integer lists only (no non-ASCII byte in this file,
--    the PAC-129 paceday_trim_ecma convention). Not STRICT, so the planner can
--    inline it (a CASE is not provably strict); NULL in, NULL out. IMMUTABLE
--    and PARALLEL SAFE: lower() under "C", translate, octet_length and
--    char_length depend on no locale or setting (lower() under the database's
--    own collation does, which is why it is not used here). Pinned against Go
--    over U+0001..U+10FFFF minus surrogates, in both directions, by the AC-21
--    test. A Go upgrade that changes its tables turns that test red; the fix
--    is a new migration that replaces the function. NO index, CHECK or
--    generated column may use this function: replacing an IMMUTABLE function
--    under one would silently corrupt it.
-- 2. operator_audit: the action list gains erase_address and
--    erase_address_dry_run. Restates all ten actions (PAC-84 contract 7.1,
--    K-9: any migration that changes the list restates it in full).

